 "notes": "CardDemo's report request (CR00, CORPT00C) on a GENERATED map input (#4506): 30 scenarios whose COMMAREA is generated and whose RECEIVE MAP input is typed for CORPT0's unprotected fields: the three report selectors, the six date parts (months 1 to 12, days 1 to 31, three years: a day past the month's end reaches the CEEDAYS refusal) and CONFIRM (Y, y, N, n or another letter); the key pressed turns through ENTER, PF3 and PF5. Proves the carddemo-report port on inputs it was not written against; the hand-written scenarios left are the fault runs, the clock-stated December wrap, the COMMAREA lengths and the named validation bounds (a month above 12 or a day above 31 is refused by the CEEDAYS model, which IBM leaves open). Derived from CardDemo (Apache-2.0; Copyright Amazon.com, Inc. or its affiliates): LICENSE and NOTICE here are the source's own.",
